        "thinking": "I'm trying to identify the root for अस्फलीः — it looks like luṅ (aorist), kartari prayoga, madhyama puruṣa eka vacana. I'm checking whether the root is स्फल् (sphala sañcalane) in bhvādi gaṇa, or possibly स्फुल् from tudādi gaṇa, since both forms exist in the dhātupāṭha with similar meanings.\n\nSince अस्फलीः doesn't show vṛddhi (which would give अस्फालीत् if it followed the standard rule for roots ending in short a + l/r), I'm reasoning that the root must belong to the kuṭādi gaṇa within tudādi — where sic is treated as ṅit, blocking vṛddhi entirely and explaining the guṇa-less form.\n\n",
